  "$schema": "fretsense/fixtures/theory/chords v1",
  "status": "PLACEHOLDER: awaiting owner + theory-checker sign-off (SC-001, tasks T009/T012/T063)",
  "why": "Derived from first principles, not from any implementation: an interval of number n moves the letter n-1 steps (C D E F G A B, cyclic); its size is the major/perfect size of that number (1:0, 2:2, 3:4, 4:5, 5:7, 6:9, 7:11, +12 per octave) adjusted by quality (perfect numbers: A +1, d -1; others: m -1, A +1, d -2). The accidental is whatever makes the new letter reach that pitch class. Any result needing |accidental| > 2 is an error (FR-010). Tables were produced by a throwaway reference script written by test-writer and spot-checked by hand against the spec examples (FR-004 D major F#, G# major F##, Gb major Cb; Edge Cases G# harmonic minor F##, A blues A C D Eb E G; FR-005 Cdim7 C Eb Gb Bbb).",
  "formulas": {
    "why": "FR-005 qualities spelled by interval: triads stack thirds (major M3+m3, minor m3+M3, dim m3+m3, aug M3+M3); sus2/sus4 replace the third with M2/P4; sevenths add m7 (dom7, min7, m7b5), M7 (maj7) or d7 (dim7, so Cdim7 has Bbb); add9 adds M9 with no seventh.",
